{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "5b2f1c6e-9a4d-4e3b-8f21-0a7c6d5e4b3a",
    "name": "llmlocal — OpenAI-compatible local LLM server",
    "description": "All endpoints of the llmlocal server (default production base http://8.231.171.198:8000).\n\n**Base URL & slash safety:** every request builds its URL from the collection variables `{{base_url}}` (origin only — NO trailing slash) and `{{api_base_url}}` (= `{{base_url}}/v1`). Never append a path that starts with `/` to a base that already ends with `/`: that combination produced `//v1/...` requests which the server (running with redirect_slashes=False) answers with 404. A collection-level pre-request script strips any trailing slash from `base_url` and rebuilds `api_base_url`, so the URL always contains exactly one slash between host, `/v1`, and the endpoint. Override `base_url` per environment (production: `http://8.231.171.198:8000`; local: `http://localhost:8000`) — see `docs/llmlocal.postman_environment.json` for a safe import template.\n\n**Interactive alternative:** the running server serves live Swagger UI at `/docs` (and ReDoc at `/redoc`) with an **Authorize** button and request-body examples pre-filled for the POST endpoints — handy for a quick manual check before scripting.\n\n**Auth setup:** set the collection variable `api_key` (or the active environment's `api_key`) to the `API_KEY` value from `.env` (any non-empty string; the server does not require a particular format). Protected requests inherit `Authorization: Bearer {{api_key}}` from the collection. Leave it empty when running in dev mode (API_KEY unset). Never commit a real key.\n\n**Worker endpoints** (`/jobs/next`, `/workers/heartbeat`) use `WORKER_TOKEN` in the query string instead — never the API key; those requests explicitly send no Authorization header. `/health`, `/docs`, `/redoc`, `/openapi.json` and `/webhooks/completions` need no credentials.\n\nSee `docs/API_EXAMPLES.md` for curl equivalents and `README.md` for the full auth model. Streaming requests (`\"stream\": true`) return `text/event-stream`; use Postman's Stream/Raw view to watch chunks — do not parse them as a single JSON body.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [ { "key": "token", "value": "{{api_key}}", "type": "string" } ]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "// Slash-safe URL construction (runs before every request in the collection).",
          "// A base_url ending in \"/\" combined with a path starting with \"/\" yields",
          "// \"//v1/...\", which the server returns as 404. Strip trailing slashes and",
          "// recompute api_base_url so every URL has exactly one slash per boundary.",
          "const origin = (pm.variables.get('base_url') || '').replace(/\\/+$/, '');",
          "if (origin) {",
          "  pm.variables.set('base_url', origin);",
          "  pm.variables.set('api_base_url', origin + '/v1');",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    { "key": "base_url", "value": "http://8.231.171.198:8000", "type": "string", "description": "Origin only (scheme://host:port) — NO trailing slash. Override per environment (e.g. http://localhost:8000)." },
    { "key": "api_base_url", "value": "{{base_url}}/v1", "type": "string", "description": "Derived from base_url. Do not edit — the collection pre-request script keeps it slash-safe." },
    { "key": "api_key", "value": "", "type": "string", "description": "Paste your .env API_KEY value here, or set it in the active environment. Never commit a real key. Required for /v1/* and /jobs, /jobs/{id}, /queue/metrics." },
    { "key": "worker_token", "value": "change-me", "type": "string", "description": "WORKER_TOKEN from .env (default placeholder shown; override if changed). Used only by /jobs/next and /workers/heartbeat." },
    { "key": "model", "value": "Qwen3-1.7B-Q4_K_M", "type": "string", "description": "Expected served model id (matches LLM_MODEL). The /v1/models test asserts it when set." },
    { "key": "job_id", "value": "", "type": "string", "description": "Set automatically by the 'Enqueue job' request." }
  ],
